WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.190 --> 00:00:05.390
Game of War took the world by storm in 2015
with a high-profile Super Bowl commercial

00:00:05.390 --> 00:00:10.909
featuring scantily clad supermodel Kate Upton—an
advertising gimmick for which developer Machine

00:00:10.909 --> 00:00:13.809
Zone reportedly paid $40 million.

00:00:13.809 --> 00:00:18.740
Since then, the online strategy game has become
one of the top-selling mobile apps in history.

00:00:18.740 --> 00:00:20.730
But what's really happening behind the scenes?

00:00:20.730 --> 00:00:24.470
Here's what you may not know about Game of
War: Fire Age.

00:00:24.470 --> 00:00:26.070
Celebrity faces

00:00:26.070 --> 00:00:31.780
After spending millions on Kate Upton's eye-catching
commercial during Super Bowl XLIX, Machine

00:00:31.780 --> 00:00:35.149
Zone went for a change of pace—and a change
of face.

00:00:35.149 --> 00:00:39.399
The next superstar to appear in a Game of
War commercial was none other than pop star

00:00:39.399 --> 00:00:40.399
Mariah Carey.

00:00:40.399 --> 00:00:42.179
"Time to be heroes, guys."

00:00:43.540 --> 00:00:48.040
The dragon-slaying diva spent a total of two
seconds on screen but reportedly earned a

00:00:48.050 --> 00:00:49.390
seven-figure paycheck.

00:00:49.390 --> 00:00:53.519
To be fair, it was still more effort than
she put into her New Year's Performance.

00:00:53.519 --> 00:00:54.519
Zing!

00:00:58.160 --> 00:00:59.540
"It just don't get any better."

00:01:00.109 --> 00:01:04.330
Of course, part of that cash probably to license
rights for her song "Hero," which is played

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:06.080
relentlessly during the ad.

00:01:06.080 --> 00:01:08.080
Was it as effective as the Kate Upton spot?

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:13.210
It's hard to say, but 2015 was definitely
a grand-slam year for Game of War according

00:01:13.210 --> 00:01:14.320
to the numbers.

00:01:14.320 --> 00:01:15.320
Cha-ching!

00:01:15.320 --> 00:01:19.780
It's not easy for a free game to bring in
a cool million a day, but it helps if you

00:01:19.780 --> 00:01:24.130
build your entire business model around getting
players to buy stuff inside the game.

00:01:24.130 --> 00:01:28.080
And if there's one thing Game of War is good
at, it's making sure its players have a reason

00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:30.780
to drop loads of cash on their virtual kingdoms.

00:01:30.780 --> 00:01:34.730
Game of War is what's known as a "freemium"
game—it's free to download and play, but

00:01:34.730 --> 00:01:38.290
if you really want to have a chance in the
game, you need to pay for the premium content.

00:01:38.290 --> 00:01:42.610
"With mobile apps, we now have the ability
to make games that are boring and stupid.

00:01:42.610 --> 00:01:45.360
But, if you pay for incentives, you're rewarded!"

00:01:45.360 --> 00:01:46.360
"Freemium.

00:01:46.360 --> 00:01:48.530
The 'mium' is Latin for 'not really.'"

00:01:48.530 --> 00:01:53.120
In fact, Game of War makes it a point to push
premium deals at just about every loading

00:01:53.120 --> 00:01:54.120
screen.

00:01:54.120 --> 00:01:57.590
Obviously, not every player—or even most
players—will spend money to get in-game

00:01:57.590 --> 00:02:01.810
advantages, but there are enough who are willing
to do just that to make Game of War one of

00:02:01.810 --> 00:02:04.370
the top-grossing mobile apps of our time.

00:02:04.370 --> 00:02:09.250
It also helps that gamers are spending way
more than the average on this app -- six times

00:02:09.250 --> 00:02:10.620
as much, in fact.

00:02:10.620 --> 00:02:16.470
According to the stats, whereas ordinary mobile
gamers spend about $86.50 to play, Game of

00:02:16.470 --> 00:02:22.470
War fans are dropping an average of $550 a
year, mostly to rack up on those gold packages

00:02:22.470 --> 00:02:26.830
that cost a whopping $99.99 apiece.

00:02:26.830 --> 00:02:28.410
"I gotta do it, man."

00:02:34.690 --> 00:02:36.020
A heaping heist

00:02:36.020 --> 00:02:41.140
Game of War is so addictive that one guy stole
$1 million to pay for his playing habits.

00:02:41.140 --> 00:02:46.410
Actually, he stole $4.8 million, but he spent
$1 million of his lifted loot on Game of War.

00:02:46.410 --> 00:02:53.260
Californian Kevin Co reportedly spent seven
years – from 2008 to 2015 – embezzling

00:02:53.260 --> 00:02:57.280
funds as an accountant for a company specializing
in construction equipment.

00:02:57.280 --> 00:03:02.080
He used most of the money for big ticket items
like cars and sports seats, your standard

00:03:02.080 --> 00:03:06.710
embezzlement candy, but somewhere along the
way he decided that a free mobile game was

00:03:06.710 --> 00:03:09.310
worth $1 million of his hard-stolen money.

00:03:09.310 --> 00:03:13.050
There's no record of exactly what he bought
in the game, but really, does it matter?

00:03:13.050 --> 00:03:16.150
That Precious Golem Ring won't help him in
prison.

00:03:16.150 --> 00:03:17.150
Critical cuts

00:03:17.150 --> 00:03:21.091
For all the money Game of War is raking in
for Machine Zone, it may be one of the most

00:03:21.091 --> 00:03:23.530
hated games of the past few years.

00:03:23.530 --> 00:03:28.270
Critics have pointed out its practically nonexistent
gameplay, the massive wait times to do anything

00:03:28.270 --> 00:03:32.950
useful, and the circular nature of the entire
system—you basically build things so you

00:03:32.950 --> 00:03:34.750
can build more things in the future.

00:03:34.750 --> 00:03:38.220
But more than anything, most critic reviews
call out Game of War as nothing more than

00:03:38.220 --> 00:03:39.720
a shameless cash grab.

00:03:39.720 --> 00:03:43.680
Basically, if you aren't a big spender, you
can spend months building your kingdom just

00:03:43.680 --> 00:03:46.040
to be slaughtered by a newcomer with deep
pockets.

00:03:46.040 --> 00:03:49.620
"Build quickly… or be destroyed quickly."

00:03:49.980 --> 00:03:53.860
But for all that hate from on high, Game of
War must be doing something right.

00:03:53.870 --> 00:03:58.731
On top of raking in more cash than some countries'
entire gross domestic products, Game of War

00:03:58.731 --> 00:04:03.560
also garnered a respectable rating on the
Google Play store from its million-plus reviewers.

00:04:03.560 --> 00:04:07.580
As much as critics seem to love hating it,
you can't argue with the numbers.

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:11.760
With over 50,000,000 downloads at this point,
Game of War is definitely popular.

00:04:11.760 --> 00:04:14.190
But how popular is it really?

00:04:14.190 --> 00:04:15.190
Well…

00:04:15.190 --> 00:04:16.190
It's still not top dog

00:04:16.190 --> 00:04:20.531
In spite of the tens of millions of dollars
Machine Zone has spent to reach the top, Game

00:04:20.531 --> 00:04:26.370
of War is still only ranked fourth in top-grossing
iPhone games, behind Candy Crush Saga, Pokemon

00:04:26.370 --> 00:04:27.990
GO, and Clash Royale.

00:04:27.990 --> 00:04:30.699
And that's pretty far behind, too, if you
go by the numbers.

00:04:30.699 --> 00:04:36.880
Although Game of War pulled in over $1 million
a day in 2015, their daily revenue has dropped

00:04:36.880 --> 00:04:42.940
to $720,000 while Clash Royale is currently
raking in over $2 million each day.

00:04:42.940 --> 00:04:44.400
Holy hell.

00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:45.850
Real world impact

00:04:45.850 --> 00:04:51.520
While Machine Zone started out as a game developer,
the company's CEO, Gabriel Leydon, has always

00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:52.520
had bigger plans.

00:04:52.520 --> 00:04:57.330
He told Bloomberg that Machine Zone is more
than just a few hundred guys building a popular

00:04:57.330 --> 00:05:01.830
mobile app, saying, "We're a technology company…we're
not really a game company."

00:05:01.830 --> 00:05:04.080
He certainly seems to be on the right track.

00:05:04.080 --> 00:05:10.830
The company rebranded itself as simply 'MZ'
in April of 2016, and in May 2016, they signed

00:05:10.830 --> 00:05:15.400
a contract with the New Zealand government
to use Game of War's technology to improve

00:05:15.400 --> 00:05:17.650
the country's public transportation.

00:05:17.650 --> 00:05:22.280
Using the system the game incorporates to
keep track of millions of players simulataneously,

00:05:22.280 --> 00:05:26.590
Leydon's real-world system will track and
manage the network structure for an entire

00:05:26.590 --> 00:05:27.590
city.

00:05:27.590 --> 00:05:32.830
"Soon the entire… entire cities will be
networked in one real-time environment, which

00:05:32.830 --> 00:05:36.260
will create a level of efficiency that the
world hasn't seen yet."

00:05:36.260 --> 00:05:38.639
Is that ambition savvy or just plain scary?

00:05:38.639 --> 00:05:40.400
You be the judge.

00:05:40.400 --> 00:05:42.000
"Krusty wants out!"

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:43.610
Thanks for watching!

00:05:43.610 --> 00:05:46.430
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:05:46.430 --> 00:05:48.910
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

